.TH SENTRY-V2CTL 8 "2026-10-28" "Sentry-v2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sentry-v2ctl \- control the sentry-v2 daemon and test policies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentry-v2ctl
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentry-v2ctl
talks to a running
.BR sentry-v2 (8)
over its control socket. The
.B policy
and
.B redact
commands read the configuration directly instead, so they work without the
daemon: in CI, on a laptop, or before the service is installed.
.PP
Reading commands need root or membership of the
.B sentry-v2
group. Commands that change something need root, or membership of both
.B sentry-v2
and
.BR sentry-v2-admin .
.SH OPTIONS
These work before or after the command.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
The control socket. Default:
.IR /run/sentry-v2/control.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of tables.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help for
.B sentry-v2ctl
or for one command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Reading
.TP
.B status
Daemon version, mode, uptime, collector health, active actions and held units.
.TP
.BR top " [" \-\-once "] [" \-\-sort " {" avg10 , cgroup }]
Cgroups under the most pressure. Refreshes every second on a terminal unless
.B \-\-once
is given. Sorted by
.B avg10
by default.
.TP
\fBincidents\fR [\fB\-\-since\fR \fITIME\fR] [\fB\-\-unit\fR \fIUNIT\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
Recent incidents, newest first.
.B \-\-since
takes an RFC 3339 time;
.B \-\-limit
defaults to 50.
.TP
.BI show " ID"
Print the bundle for one incident as JSON.
.TP
.B actions
Active throttles and freezes, then recent action records.
.TP
.B policies
Loaded policies with their effective mode, and the last reload error if any.
.SS Changing
.TP
.BR rollback " {" \fIID\fR | \-\-all }
Undo one action now, or every active one. Any unique 6 or more characters
from the start or end of an action id will do.
.TP
.BI ack " UNIT"
Let a unit held for acting too often be acted on again.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume
Force dry-run for new actions while everything else keeps running, and turn
that off again.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read the configuration and policies, like
.BR "systemctl reload sentry-v2" .
.TP
.BI restore " UNIT/YYYYmmddTHHMMSSZ"
Put back the files a
.B backup_reload
action saved. Checks every file before writing any; doesn't reload the unit
itself.
.SS Offline
These take
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
(default
.IR /etc/sentry-v2/sentry-v2.toml )
and
.BI \-\-policies " DIR"
(default
.IR /etc/sentry-v2/policies.d ).
.TP
.B policy validate
Check the configuration and policies.
.TP
.BI "policy test \-\-event" " FILE"
Feed a JSON event, a list of events, or a bundle saved by the daemon through
the correlator and the policies, and print the actions that would be
planned.
.TP
.BR redact " [" \fIFILE\fR ]
Print what the configured redaction leaves of
.IR FILE ,
or of stdin when it's left out or
.BR \- .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed: an invalid configuration, an error from the daemon, or an
unreadable file.
.TP
.B 2
The daemon isn't running, or the command line was wrong.
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied, on the socket or by the daemon.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, status words aren't coloured.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sentry-v2ctl status
sentry-v2ctl \-\-json incidents \-\-limit 10
sentry-v2ctl show 0199f2a1\-8150\-7d44\-a2b6\-0c1d2e3f4a5b
sentry-v2ctl policy test \-\-event /tmp/fail.json
echo 'app \-\-password hunter2' | sentry-v2ctl redact
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sentry-v2 (8)
.PP
The full CLI guide:
.UR https://github.com/jamesconwaydev/sentry-v2/blob/main/docs/cli.md
docs/cli.md
.UE
